<title>USA: Amarillo feeder cattle prices up $1-$2 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Amarillo feeder cattle prices up $1-$2 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>AMARILLO 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Feeder steers and heifers were $1.00-$2.00 per cwt higher, compared to last week, USDA said.</p>
<p>Bulk supply Medium and Large 1- 2 300-800 lb feeder steers and heifers. Trade moderate. Demand fairly good. Feeder steers and heifers under 600 lbs 46 percent, over 600 lbs 52 percent with cows and bulls around 2 percent of total supply.</p>
<p>Feeder Steers - Medium and Large 1 - 600-700 lbs</p>
<p>76.50-81.50, pkg 636 lbs thin 85.50; 700-800 lbs 71.00-75.75, part load 765 lbs thin 77.00; pkg 829 lbs 72.00; load 975 lbs 65.25. Medium and Large 1-2 - 600-700 lbs 68.00-74.75; few 700-800 lbs 64.00-68.50.</p>
<p>Feeder Heifers - Medium and Large 1 - 600-700 lbs</p>
<p>71.25-75.25, pkg 620 lbs thin 77.00; 700-800 lbs 66.75-72.00;</p>
<p>few 837-857 lbs 64.40-66.75.. Medium and Large 1-2 - 600-700 lbs 68.00-69.75.</p>
<p>Receipts - 2,762    Week Ago - 1,343   Year Ago - 1,390</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
